From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: powershell: a script the stub cannot run fails

Wine's powershell.exe runs nothing, and exited 0 for every script. That
answered electron-builder's NSIS installers (Joplin, Obsidian and most
Electron applications) "yes" to 'is Get-CimInstance available?' and then
to 'is the application already running?': they could not close it and quit
with exit code 2, installing nothing.

A -Command/-File/-EncodedCommand script, or a positional command, now exits
1 -- what PowerShell returns for a failed command -- so callers take their
fallback (electron-builder's is tasklist | findstr, which works). A script
that is just 'exit N' returns N; '-Command -' reading stdin and no script at
all still exit 0.

Gate: test/powershell-gate.sh.
